      "writtenOn": "2022-11-12T03:29:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Lorenzo, please check the String.format performance issue here:\nhttps://g3doc.corp.google.com/gws/g3doc/user/performance/tips/java.md?cl\u003dhead\n\n\"String.format() is OK for rarely executed code like log messages. It should not be used for regular processing. Every time String.format() is called, it uses a regular expression to parse the format String.\nString.format() is ok for exceptions, one-time initialization, and complex formatting. It should be avoided in code that is frequently processed. Logger\u0027s formatting methods should be used for formatting because the Logger will defer formatting until the log message clears the severity level. For frequent log messages, it may be better to avoid the formatting and just append the output.\"\n\n\nAlso please check the performance profiling result in here:\nhttps://pprof.corp.google.com/?id\u003df62e3fde08a7af95a93076651001cc5d\u0026tab\u003dflame\u0026path\u003d103kebk0plnruf\u0026metric\u003dcpu-cycles\u0026pivot\u003dWifiConfigManager.addOrUpdateNetwork\nThe flame diagram shows the MacAddress.toString uses significant of CPU cycles.\n\nWill add some comment in the code to explain the change. thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "8cc5be61_9542afea",
      "revId": "87be2791c48a05147be904ab128cc6f25eb0489c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
